 stories like that I write about and  including Brenda Carter who after 13  years in the same job and in Human  Resources was fired and she describes  the moment of going to her office where  she had her life you know her life of 13  years from pictures to plants collecting  everything and not being able to find  another job so she's now making cookies  and selling them online and you know the  stories are endless like I mean there  isn't a way it's important to put flesh  and blood on the numbers it's because  that's how we connect with what is  happening it's hard to really connect  with 26 million people being out of work  or underemployed but the stories speak  to us but those stories are also stories  of resilience yes and comebacks and  what's great about America I love that  you know I have a series of steps in the  book of what we can do to move away from  despair and into action because I really  completely believe in that and the first  is tap into your own resilience because  we all have it anyway we've all been  through hard times and we know the  difference between tapping into that  resilience tapping into our own inner  strength and and when we don't so that's  step number one no matter what my mom  has always said to me everybody in this  life will be thrown curveballs it's not  about the curveball it's about how you  catch it how your handle the curveball  that is so  your mom is very wise we wanted to write  about it on half past because we're  collecting the stories because in a  sense I see the book as the beginning of  this conversation  so tap into your own resilience then  share your story because there is power  in sharing our stories you know you're  sharing your mom's story I sharing what  I went through I tell my daughters  they're sick of hearing it my second  book was rejected by 36 publishers  because you know I could have given up  but not number 25 right of the  rejections and said that's 18 I'm not a  writer  I should go to something else and so  that so tap into your resilience share  your story then the third thing is  improve your financial literacy because  a lot of people don't really know how to  deal with their mortgages their credit  cards the way the banks have always  hidden fees overdraft fees penalties and  now there is this amazing group that I  write about called hello wallet calm for  five dollars a month  it can provide financial advice so there  are these groups that are springing up  that can actually use the resources  available online to educate people well  one thing that I found is unfortunately  nobody ever teaches you about their  death so as a child we don't learn it  you really need that from home just a  basic about money why do you have to  save I mean that alone and then you grow  up and you're too embarrassed to tell  people I have no idea what you're  talking about I know and then you're  presented with this 30 page contracts  for your credit card or I don't know how  many pages as soon as you go to college  they ask you to take a credit card yeah  exactly and then you have these teaser  rates and then skyrocketing interest  rates and again you mentioned at the  beginning that I write how this didn't  just happen overnight you know you go  back to the late 1970s when it became  possible for credit cards  to be registered anywhere and just  charge the interest rates of that state  so Delaware for example have and that is  usually laws so credit card companies  could charge 29 and 30 percent interest  rates and you didn't even know it and  you didn't even know it because it's the  fine print exactly and you were given a  teaser rate so learning about all that  and learning about all these people who  are offering you things don't have your  best interests at heart learning about  all the tricks and traps it's absolutely  critical and educating our children  about it and one thing that I love about  what you write in the book and also what  you write all the time in HuffPost is  the fact that these are not right or  left interviews this is not about  politics it's not about politics and it  doesn't matter if you're a Republican or  a Democrat we all want the same things  for our families and we all nobody wants  to be taken in and you talk about saving  you know right now the saving rate for  people this is so minuscule that how do  we save again people are saving more and  more but how can we actually have a real  saving rate so you actually can make  some money from saving all these things  are things that are going to be  incredibly important as we are moving  inevitably away from a consumption based  society to a society based on on  different values people are really a  ting their lives right now after what  we've been through yes if there's one  thing that the Obama administration can  do to ensure we do not see this great  country become third world America what  would it be  Maria it has to be about jobs there's no  question about that but really about  jobs not rhetorically about jobs it has  to be bringing that same mindset and  that existed during the financial  meltdown when everybody came together  and say  basically metaphorically were not  leaving this room until we saved the  financial system there has to be the  same attitude so throwing everything  against the wall from infrastructure  projects to payroll tax holidays to  encouraging innovation to encouraging  and entrepreneurs who can create jobs  wherever they're coming from all that  has to be the highest priority and that  includes ending our engagement in  Afghanistan ending this kind of perverse  priorities that are draining our  resources and and being so detrimental  to our future and you and let's not  forget that payroll tax holiday that  you're talking about we encourage people  to keep more of their money and  ultimately what do they do they spend it  exactly and you know just to complete  what we were saying about the steps  going down to the growing of financial  literacy and move your money we launched  the project that we're calling move your  money so that people recognize that they  have the power to move the money from  from big banks that have cut lending and  move their money into smaller community  banks credit unions that are much more  likely to reinvest in their communities  and that's in our power to do this book  is as much about America and  institutions as it is that individuals  yes having the power to change things  Breanna congratulations thank you so  much good to talk to you third world  America how our politicians are  abandoning the middle class and  betraying the American Dream by Arianna  Huffington
 

